    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nEach additional cursor is invisible when hlsearch is on and the cursor is placed inside of the highlighted region. I thought it could have been my colorscheme but this issue persists with the default colorscheme on latest master.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean\n:set hlsearch\n(enter some searchable text)\n/search query\nQnQnQn\nYou should see that the additional cursors are not visible\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nEach cursor is visible inside of the highlighted region\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1489+gf1d89e874a\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNot applicable\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nCentos 8\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ngnome-terminal v3.28.3, VTE 0.52.4\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-265color\n\n### Installation\n\nMaster, from source",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is not only an issue with search. Several \"built-in\" highlighting mechanisms are always above extmark highlighting: search, spelling (like if `hi MCursor guisp=Blue gui=underline`, then it will be invisible on spelling error), `:match`, etc.\n\nRelated: #18756.\n\nIt would be good for those built-in highlighting to also have a fixed (maybe separate per \"source\") `zindex`, so that extmarks may choose to be on top of those.",
